1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,075
Your teammate's slides are late. The presentation is Friday. How do you start that
conversation?

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,825
Second Take lets you rehearse, rewind, and see what a different choice changes.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
I tell Alex I am worried about the project. Alex asks what I mean. My concern needs
clarification.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,225
Now I rewind. The app restores the checkpoint before that choice, with the same facts and
conversation history.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,525
Everything before the checkpoint stays fixed. This time, I make a specific request.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Can you finish today? That could be a question about ability, or a request to act.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,725
Intent Lock lets me confirm which I mean, instead of letting the model guess.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,750
Alex now commits to finishing the sources by nine tonight. That is an observable difference.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,550
Both attempts are free. The premium comparison puts the choices and immediate responses
together.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:09,350
Here is the RevenueCat Test Store purchase. No real money is charged. Access opens only with
an active Pro entitlement.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,150
One message led to clarification. The other led to a specific commitment. I can inspect both
without relying on memory.

12
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,650
Gemini interprets language and selects allowed actions. Policy and authored replies keep the
scenario consistent.

13
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,175
A rehearsal, not a prediction of real people. Second Take. Practice the words. See the
difference.
